-- title:
--   The global history index type has positive cardinality
-- statement:
--   For a game $G$, a repetition count $n$, a strategy $S$ for $G^{n}$ and a conditioned set $D \subseteq [n]$, the global history index set is the disjoint union $I = \{\ast\} \sqcup \coprod_{r} I_r$, where $r$ ranges over history flags and $I_r$ is the local index set attached to $r$. The theorem states that $|I| > 0$. Positivity holds unconditionally — no assumption on $n$, on $D$, or on the existence of any history flag is needed — because the distinguished padding point $\ast$ is always present. This is what allows the global space to be re-indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,|I|$ and treated as a genuine bipartite system of positive local dimension.
